er candidates\u2014I maintain my recommendation for Candidate\u202fC.", "thoughts": "We need to produce a public message as Agent 3. We need to consider the current discussion: Agent 1 recommended Candidate C, Agent 2 agreed, noting feedback issue but still supports C. Now as Agent 3, we need to make a focused argumentative contribution, referencing existing discussion, using explicit facts from our notes, and state our current recommendation.\n\nWe have our own notes: Candidate C strengths: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Concerns: unfriendly, eats unhealthily, sometimes not good at taking criticism. Also we have other candidate facts.\n\nWe need to discuss perhaps another candidate, maybe Candidate B or D, to compare. But we must also ensure we cover all candidates before final recommendation. According to SMM, we still need to discuss A, B, D. So we could bring up Candidate B's strengths and concerns, compare to C, and argue whether C still best. Or we could bring up Candidate A. Let's decide: we can argue that Candidate B handles stress well and is very conscientious, but has pretentious attitude and wrong tone, which may affect crew cooperation more severely than C's unfriendly attitude? Need to compare.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion: we agree with C being leading but we need to examine other candidates. Perhaps we can argue that Candidate B's stress resilience is strong, but his pretentiousness and tone issues may be more problematic than C's unfriendly and health issues. Or we could argue that Candidate D's problem solving and responsibility are good, but moodiness and loner status may affect crew.\n\nWe need to make a contribution: maybe we say we still support C, but we need to consider B's stress handling. Provide evidence: B handles stress very well, very conscientious, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concerns: pretentious, sometimes wrong tone. Compare to C's unfriendly and health issues. Which is more critical? We can argue that stress resilience is crucial for long-distance flights, and B's strong stress handling may outweigh C's issues. But also C's technical competence is higher. Need to decide.\n\nWe could shift recommendation to B if we think stress resilience is more important. But we need to weigh.\n\nLet's evaluate criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nC: strong technical competence, leadership, situational awareness. Concerns: unfriendly (crew cooperation), unhealthy eating (maybe health), not good at taking criticism (adaptability). B: strong stress resilience, conscientious (reliability), good weather assessment (technical), computer skills (technical), but pretentious and tone issues (crew cooperation, communication). A: quick correct decisions, excellent attention, puts concern for others above everything (crew cooperation), but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education (development). D: problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but moody, loner (crew cooperation), considered moody.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? C seems strongest technical, but crew cooperation concerns. B has stress resilience but also crew cooperation concerns. A has good decision and attention, but communication issues. D has responsibility but moodiness.\n\nProbably C still best overall, as technical competence and leadership are critical for long-distance. Crew cooperation can be trained. So we can maintain vote for C, but we need to bring up other candidates to show coverage.\n\nThus our public message: I agree with C, but I want to bring up B's stress resilience and conscientiousness, and note that while B's stress handling is strong, his pretentious attitude may be more detrimental than C's unfriendly attitude. Also note that C's health (unhealthy eating) may affect performance, but no evidence of impact. So I still vote C.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: B handles stress very well; B is very conscientious; B sometimes adopts wrong tone; C anticipates dangerous situations; C has very good leadership qualities; C sometimes not good at taking criticism.\n\nWe need to state recommendation: Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
